tic sequence is given by:\n\\[a_n = a_1 + (n-1)d\\]\nwhere \\(a_n\\) is the \\(n\\)-th term, \\(a_1\\) is the first term, \\(d\\) is the common difference, and \\(n\\) is the number of terms.\n\nFor our sequence:\n- The first term \\(a_1 = 2008\\)\n- The common difference \\(d = -5\\)\n- The last term \\(a_n = 3\\)\n\nWe need to find \\(n\\), the number of terms. Using the formula for the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence:\n\\[a_n = a_1 + (n-1)d\\]\nwe substitute the known values:\n\\[3 = 2008 + (n-1)(-5)\\]\nSimplify the equation:\n\\[3 = 2008 - 5(n-1)\\]\n\\[3 = 2008 - 5n + 5\\]\n\\[3 = 2013 - 5n\\]\nRearrange to solve for \\(n\\):\n\\[5n = 2013 - 3\\]\n\\[5n = 2010\\]\n\\[n = \\frac{2010}{5}\\]\n\\[n = 402\\]\n\nThus, the number of terms in the list is \\(\\boxed{402}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{402}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"prealgebra:614"}
